From: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu Sep 24 13:39:52 2026 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: Add GCC CX power domain

The GCC GDSCs on SM8250 are backed by the RPMh CX power domain. Without
describing that parent domain, consumers of GCC-provided GDSCs can enable
their local domain without causing the required CX vote to be held.

Add the CX power-domain reference to the GCC node so votes from GCC GDSC
consumers can propagate to RPMh CX.

Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260924-qcom-tie-cx-to-gcc-v5-36-38732033e5b5@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

(cherry picked from upstream commit 389a0144c511316cf21d5dc2aa30028de87f9d00, first released in v7.4-rc1;
 applies to v7.3.4 without changes)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
index fae8382349..16348b0538 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -971,6 +971,7 @@
 			clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>,
 				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>,
 				 <&sleep_clk>;
+			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_CX>;
 		};
 
 		ipcc: mailbox@408000 {
